# Project Overview
- **Stack:** Next.js App Router (v15), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, SWR, Prisma (PostgreSQL/Neon), NextAuth.js.
- **Purpose:** Suggest random “beautiful” airports (Small/Medium/Large) from a seeded list, let users mark them visited, and view/clear their history.

# Key Files & Folders
- `prisma/schema.prisma` & `prisma/seed.js` – Data model & seeding from `prisma/airports.json`.
- `src/app/api/airport/` – CRUD endpoints:  
  – `random/route.ts`  
  – `visit/route.ts`  
  – `clear/route.ts`  
  – `visited/route.ts`
- `src/app/auth/` –  
  – `signin/page.tsx`  
  – `signup/page.tsx`
- `src/app/page.tsx` – Home page component.
- `src/app/visited/page.tsx` – Visited airports list.
- `src/app/layout.tsx` – Global layout & header (Home / Visited / Logout).

# Coding Guidelines
- **Components:** Functional React + hooks only; client components (`'use client'`) for SWR.
- **Data Fetching:** Use `useSWR` pointed at `/api/...` endpoints.
- **Styling:** Tailwind utility-first. Use the existing container/grid pattern from Home and Visited pages.
- **API Routes:**  
  – Always export `GET`, `POST` (or other verbs) from `route.ts` files.  
  – Use `NextResponse.json()` with proper HTTP status.  
  – Protect with NextAuth’s `getSession()` or `getServerSession()`.

# Database & Auth
- **Prisma Models:**  
  – `User` with `visitedAirports` relation.  
  – `Airport` with `airportCode`, `icaoCode`, etc.  
- **Auth:** Credentials provider via NextAuth.js.  
  – Sign-in with email/username + password.  
  – Sign-up creates & auto-signs in new users.

# Naming & Structure
- Pages in `src/app/{path}`:  
  – `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, and nested `/api/.../route.ts`.
- Keep filenames lowercase with dashes.
- Always handle missing or unauthorized cases gracefully.

# UX Patterns
- “Get Random” / “Mark as Visited” / “Clear Visited” buttons.
- Responsive center-column card layout.
- Redirect unauthenticated users to `/auth/signin`.

# Workflows
- **Seeding:** `npx prisma migrate dev && npm run prisma:seed`
- **Local Dev:** `npm run dev`
- **Build:** `npm run build`
- **Deploy:** Vercel or any Next.js-compatible host.

> Whenever Cursor performs edits or answers, use these rules to keep suggestions aligned with our existing code style, architecture, and project conventions.
